  "checks": [
    "The existing proved interiorCompletion PartB supplies the original actual typed-atlas Airy coefficients (1,0,-xi). Its only changed field is dividedDifference, so the principal conclusion is definitionally about the same old K. No final whole-atlas geometry/primitive certificate is an input.",
    "The whole record negative-fields equality retains exactly the original cutPair index, canonical endpoints, coefficient field and sample. The actual unit point belongs to its true canonical open piece because rho>0 and 0<u<1.",
    "The four actual atoms equal 1,1,0,-rho*u on the open unit strip. This equality yields actual ContDiffOn, period and every mixed derivative through the genuine open-set derivative congruence; it does not assert equality of arbitrary total extensions.",
    "The exact original half canonical-length upper bound is transported only through the explicit enlargement U=enlargedMaterialData T. Original E0 is used only with its true positivity, never a unit lower bound.",
    "One coefficient B is selected before every new enumeration, positive field family, state, piece, atom and derivative order. The bound is valid at all actual valid states and therefore includes reference state.",
    "All actual source, provider and pinned API identities were recorded; no source/compiler/CI/index/ref/checkpoint/authority mutation occurred."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "Only the four negative principal atoms are covered, not the negative potential, full-half height tower, positive principal atoms or the complete 33-atom certificate.",
    "The atlas is constructed using the original T. The explicit material enlargement is used for these four atom bounds and the right-hand sample envelope; all four atoms are independent of the material record.",
    "Same-witness Through03, hfield and actual return-margin length provider are retained. No new raw optical lower bound, cell uniqueness or whole-positive common cell is assumed."
